   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">BII has provided a $40 million commitment to Indorama in Nigeria to enable its subsidiaries (Indorama Eleme Fertilizers and Chemical Limited and Indorama Eleme Petrochemicals Limited) to purchase equipment and implement processes that reduce greenhouse gases, recover heat and improve effluent treatment. This will support Indorama to reduce its emissions and increase water-use efficiency.The investment will support Indorama to reduce emissions at its Nigerian fertiliser plants by up to 348 million tCO2e per annum by 2026 (a 15 per cent reduction from its 2022 baseline). Our funding will also help the business reduce its annual water consumption by 635m3/hour, easing pressure on groundwater aquifers.</narrative>
   </description>
